---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import {
  HoverCardInText,
  HoverCardPlayground,
} from "../../components/HoverCardDemo";
---

<Docs
  title="Hover Card"
  description="A preview card for links to people, projects, and pages."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Hover Card</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    A small card that previews what a link points to. It opens when the link is
    hovered or keyboard-focused. Use it for a profile or a page summary; the
    link itself must still work without it.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8" id="hover-card-demo">
    <HoverCardPlayground client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Hover card usage"
      code={`import {
  HoverCard,
  HoverCardContent,
  HoverCardTrigger,
} from "@tulipfarm/sprout/hover-card";

<HoverCard>
  <HoverCardTrigger render={<a href="/people/alex" />}>
    Alex Meadow
  </HoverCardTrigger>
  <HoverCardContent side="top">
    <p className="font-medium">Alex Meadow</p>
    <p className="text-sm text-sprout-muted">
      Fictional garden project coordinator.
    </p>
  </HoverCardContent>
</HoverCard>`}
    />
    <p>
      Pass your link or router link to <code>HoverCardTrigger</code> through <code
        >render</code
      >. Without it the trigger renders a plain <code>a</code>. Put a name in
      the first line of the card and a muted description below it.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Mentions in text</h2>
    <p>
      Hover cards sit inside running text. Use <code>align="start"</code> to line
      the card up with the start of the name. Long names wrap inside the 16rem card,
      and the card shrinks to fit narrow screens.
    </p>
    <HoverCardInText client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section" id="hover-card-api">
    <h2 class="section-title">API</h2>
    <p>
      <code>HoverCard</code> wraps the Base UI preview card root and takes <code
        >open</code
      >, <code>defaultOpen</code>, <code>onOpenChange</code>, and <code
        >actionsRef</code
      >.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>HoverCardTrigger</code> takes <code>render</code>, <code>delay</code
      > (600ms), <code>closeDelay</code> (300ms), and every anchor prop.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>HoverCardContent</code> renders its own portal and positioner. It takes
      <code>side</code> (<code>"bottom"</code>), <code>align</code> (<code
        >"center"</code
      >), <code>sideOffset</code> (4), <code>alignOffset</code> (4), <code
        >collisionPadding</code
      > (8), <code>anchor</code>, <code>keepMounted</code>, <code
        >container</code
      >, and every Base UI popup prop. Each part sets a <code>data-slot</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The card opens on hover and on keyboard focus, and closes on Escape, blur,
      or pointer leave. Screen readers read the link, not the card, so the card
      should only repeat or add to what the link’s page shows.
    </p>
    <p>
      Cards fade, scale, and slide in from their side over 120ms. Motion turns
      off when reduced motion is requested. In forced-colors mode the card keeps
      a visible border.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Hover cards use <code>--sprout-surface</code>, <code>--sprout-line</code>,
      <code>--sprout-text</code>, <code>--sprout-muted</code>, <code
        >--sprout-shadow-overlay</code
      >, and the panel radius. The link uses <code>--sprout-border</code> for its
      underline and <code>--sprout-focus</code> for its focus ring. They need no brand
      color, so they look the same with the neutral and TulipFarm themes in light
      and dark mode.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
